        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Support Vector Machine 0.71 0.718 1.000 0.836" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics15151859> ;
            slr:claim_label "The SVM comparator has recall 1.000 at precision 0.718 - the all-positive classifier - so 0.71 is the majority-class baseline, printed in the comparison table without being identified as such." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Each scanpath was converted into a fixed-length representation by truncating or zero-padding the first N_fix = 20 fixations." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.2> ;
            slr:claim_label "A 20-fixation cap discards later fixations in longer scanpaths and pads shorter ones; its effect on the result is not tested." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.82"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The results obtained from our research indicate that it is preferable to have a dataset where the data obtained relates to ASD children and not neurotypical subjects, specifically, when the task is to predict the values for valence and arousal." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:0a8191e6e542> ;
            slr:claim_label "A clean cross-population transfer result: affect models built on neurotypical faces do not generalise to autistic children, and fine-tuning on autistic data materially improves them. This bears on every study in the corpus that applies a generic emotion-recognition model to autistic people." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.96"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "After this analytics step, it is vital to the machine learning model to split the data. The benefit of this is to prevent overfitting of the data by training the model on a majority of the data and testing its accuracy on a small portion of it" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:0c3188260dff> ;
            slr:claim_label "Data splitting is described as occurring after feature selection, placing supervised selection outside the validation loop while presenting the split as protection against overfitting." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "All the ASD participants were diagnosed by the experienced Chinese psychiatrists based on the psychoeducational profile (Third Edition) and Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders-V criteria." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:3ba88bcdc38e> ;
            slr:claim_label "Diagnosis relied on psychiatrist judgement under DSM-5 with PEP-3 support, rather than on ADOS or ADI-R." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
