            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "IQ (Mean +/- SD) 100.8 +/- 22.7 [ASD] 116.1 +/- 22.7 [TD] t(37) = 2.45 .019" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10803-022-05685-x> ;
            slr:claim_label "The groups differ significantly in non-verbal IQ, an uncontrolled confound for a task whose sole discriminative feature is the dispersion of gaze during a demanding conversation." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.87"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "While language indices were significantly associated with performance of several models, ADOS scores and IQ were never significantly associated with classification in any model. This suggests that our methodology captures specific communication characteristics associated with autism that are unconfounded by cognitive level and autism severity." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1002/aur.2733> ;
            slr:claim_label "The IQ imbalance was tested rather than merely acknowledged, and IQ never predicted misclassification in any of the three models." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Importantly, of the two games, the more effective one involved only free-style colouring with no specific gameplay pattern. This confirms motor pattern, and not differences in attention to particular elements of gameplay, is a significant differentiating factor." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/srep31107> ;
            slr:claim_label "The unstructured free-play game outperformed the structured one, which the authors read as evidence the signal is motor rather than attentional." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "due to the low number of participants in creating the dataset and the short duration of the video scenarios, more extended scenarios should be allowed to obtain images with more information in both classes. Likewise, the amount of information in the images and the use of space in the ''x'' and ''y'' coordinates are essential factors when classifying ASD" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:3dc286a9aa92> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors identify image information density and spatial coverage as the operative factors, which is a plot-density property rather than a behavioural one." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "we implemented K-means clustering algorithm in the eye tracking dataset and generated several clusters where the instances of ASD and non-ASD groups were more correlated. So, individual classifiers were grouped into these instances more efficiently than primary data." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/ICREST51555.2021.9331152> ;
            slr:claim_label "The reported improvement is attributed to clustering producing groups in which the classes are more separable, without any characterisation of what the clusters represent." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The ﬁnal diagnosis was based on the best clinical estimate diagnosis according to the DSM-5 ASD criteria by a licensed child psychiatrist using all of the available participant information." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:63f4f1af3671> ;
            slr:claim_label "Diagnostic labels came from a licensed child psychiatrist's DSM-5 best-estimate diagnosis integrating seven assessment instruments." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "For the training and testing of the proposed algorithm, 80 % of the dataset was allocated for training purposes while the remaining 20 % was used for performance validation." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:c846224c5959> ;
            slr:claim_label "The only statement of evaluation design: an image-level split over 1,500 images from 30 children with roughly 50 images each and no participant-level partitioning, so recognising the child recovers the fixed severity label and 98.33% is the arithmetic of the arrangement." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.98"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Video coding was completed by 2 trained graduate students, and the duration and frequency of the 5 indicators during the FF and SF episodes were calculated. ... the ICCs for protest behavior, non-social smiling, eye contact, social smiling, and active social engagement were 0.76, 0.82, 0.81, 0.83, and 0.79, respectively." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fped.2020.00290> ;
            slr:claim_label "Features were produced by human coders rather than automated sensing, with inter-coder reliability quantified per behaviour." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "ASD diagnosis was made according to Diagnostic Statistical Manual- IV-R (DSM-IV-R) [5], [6] diagnostic criteria while ADHD diagnosis is based on Schedule for Affective Disorders and Schizophrenia for School-Age Children-Present and Lifetime Version (K-SADS-PL) [7] Turkish version is used for the evaluation [8]." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:f7f1df920e13> ;
            slr:claim_label "Autism was confirmed by DSM-IV-R criteria and ADHD by the Turkish K-SADS-PL; no ADOS or ADI-R was used." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The cluster numbers were tuned for different experiments to reach the best accuracy. The cluster numbers were, respectively, set to 16, 64, and 96 for the same-race, other-race, and all faces in the current model." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:752eeff1ddb3> ;
            slr:claim_label "The number of K-means clusters was tuned per experiment to maximise accuracy on the evaluation data." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Some videos also included a live host who interacted verbally with the child, trying to guide their focus towards both seen and hidden elements." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/info15030133> ;
            slr:claim_label "The source protocol included a live host verbally directing attention, so the recorded scan-paths reflect responsiveness to social instruction as well as spontaneous visual preference - a detail absent from the other reuses of this dataset and relevant to what the classifier separates." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.87"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Spatial eye-gaze representations in the form of scanpaths in stratifying ASD and TD (ASD vs. TD: DNN: 74.4%) are feasible. These spatial eye-gaze features, e.g., scan-paths, are shown to be sensitive to factors mediating heterogeneity in ASD: age (ASD: 2-4 y/old vs. 10-17 y/old CNN: 80.5%), gender (Male vs. Female ASD: DNN: 78.0%) and the mixture of age and gender (5-9 y/old Male vs. 5-9 y/old Female ASD: DNN:98.8%)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1145/3539226> ;
            slr:claim_label "The study's own experiments show scan-path images classify age band and sex within the autistic group more accurately than they classify diagnosis - direct internal evidence that this representation encodes demographics at least as strongly as autism." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.99"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We reviewed the top 20 important features based upon their SHAP values within each fold. There was a high level of overlap between the top 20 features, with 15 (65%) in all three folds, 6 (25%) in two folds, and 3 (12.5%) unique to a specific fold, out of the total 24 unique features across the three folds." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:71fd566a4ffb> ;
            slr:claim_label "Feature-importance stability is quantified across folds rather than a single ranking being presented as a property of the data - a discipline almost absent from this corpus and one that determines how much weight an importance ranking can bear." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.92"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve was used to evaluate the predictive performance of the model, which revealed a good prediction performance with the area under the curve (AUC) of 0.826 (95% CI: 0.776-0.877) ... The optimal cutoff value of the ROC curve was 0.399, with a sensitivity of 85.4%, specificity of 68.3%, positive predictive value (PPV) of 72.9%, and negative predictive value (NPV) of 82.4%." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s12888-024-06129-9> ;
            slr:claim_label "Modest, plausible performance reported with an interval and with both predictive values - a different register from the 95-100% accuracies typical of this corpus. The threshold was chosen from this same curve, and the predictive values hold only at the matched 50% prevalence." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "in conclusion, all presented studies, adopted machine learning differently yet there is no automatic prediction model integrated within a screening tool to be used in clinics." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:6a3b6c2a276b> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors identify the absence of any automatic prediction model embedded within a deployable clinical screening tool as the field's gap." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Toddlers between 17-36 months of age were recruited at four pediatric primary care clinics during their well-child visit. Toddlers received a commonly-used, caregiver-completed autism screening questionnaire, Modified Checklist for Autism in Toddler - Revised with Follow-up (M-CHAT-R/F) as part of routine clinical care. If a child screened positive on the M-CHAT-R/F, or a caregiver/clinician expressed any developmental concern, the child was evaluated by a child psychologist based on the Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule - Toddler (ADOS-T) module." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:665e8c7a855d> ;
            slr:claim_label "Prospective ascertainment inside routine primary care with universal screening and ADOS-T evaluation - a screening cohort at 9.2% prevalence rather than a specialist-clinic case-control contrast, and the strongest sampling frame in this review." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.98"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "while we require parents to disclose their child's clinical diagnosis by choosing from options not widely known to those who have not received a clinical evaluation, these labels are self-reported and thus unverified." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:44d2304739ef> ;
            slr:claim_label "Diagnostic labels rest on unverified parent report, as the authors concede." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "This paper trained the model using 10 rounds of cross-validation, with 100 epochs and a 20% dropout rate. The kernel size used was 3, and the stride initially set to 1 but later changed to 2." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/info15030133> ;
            slr:claim_label "Cross-validation is applied to the 547 images with no statement that a child's roughly nine images were kept within a fold, and is simultaneously the selection criterion for more than a hundred hyperparameter configurations reported across twelve tables." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.96"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The next step in our model is Filter Based Feature Selection. The specific scoring model used during this step was Mutual Information... Through this step we were able to identify the top 6 attributes in this dataset, and excluded all others in future steps." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:0c3188260dff> ;
            slr:claim_label "Supervised mutual-information feature selection was applied to the whole dataset, reducing 16 attributes to 6." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "To illustrate that the classification accuracy was higher than the chance level, results on majority class prediction are also plotted as a comparison. In majority class prediction, every behavior was classified as the category with higher percentage in quantity." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10803-022-05685-x> ;
            slr:claim_label "An empirically derived majority-class chance floor is computed at every window length, correctly acknowledging that the segment-level class imbalance is group-linked - better practice on chance level than most studies in this corpus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.88"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Our experiments indicate that we can get 65.41% accuracy on the validation dataset." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:10ab04b596b1> ;
            slr:claim_label "The best internal validation accuracy was 65.41%." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Informed consent was obtained from the subject in Fig 1, their legal guardian and the examiner for the publication of identifying information/images in an online open-access publication." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:dac3e7a03f26> ;
            slr:claim_label "Separate specific consent for publication of an identifying image, from the child, the guardian and the examiner - a level of consent detail no other included study reports, and the direct counterpoint to the studies charted nearby that train on children's photographs scraped from support pages with no ethics statement at all." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.86"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Considering the small size of our dataset, we performed leave-one-out cross validation (LOOCV)... Initially, we classified the n-th data as test data and the remaining data as training data Dtrain. Following this, we trained the tag annotation model using Dtrain. The trained tag annotation model was then used to automatically annotate xn" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:e15a1551c489> ;
            slr:claim_label "The automatic annotation model - a fitted preprocessing component - is retrained inside each cross-validation fold rather than once on the whole corpus, so annotations of held-out participants are produced by a model that never saw them. Almost no other study in this corpus identifies this as a leakage route." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.97"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The same hyperparameter settings were used to train all the models to facilitate a fair comparison of them: VGG16, CNN-LSTM, MobileNet, CNN-GRU and EfficientNet-B7." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fncom.2026.1626315> ;
            slr:claim_label "All five architectures were trained under identical settings - one of the few genuinely controlled architecture comparisons in the charted corpus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.88"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Results showed that the KNN algorithm (k = 1) yielded the highest classiﬁcation accuracy with four kinematic features (accuracy: 88.37%, speciﬁcity: 91.3%, sensitivity: 85%, AUC: 0.8815)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:ea9c4425e2e9> ;
            slr:claim_label "A 1-nearest-neighbour classifier with four kinematic features achieved 88.37% accuracy and AUC 0.8815." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We recruited 140 children with ASD (112 boys and 28 girls) between 3 to 6 years of age (mean (M) = 4.66, standard deviation (SD) = 1.00) and 193 TD children (122 boys and 71 girls) between 3 to 6 years of age (M = 4.77, SD = 0.92) for the test. All the subjects participating in the test had normal vision or corrected vision." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:5e6c6c482e7c> ;
            slr:claim_label "The entire participant description: no diagnostic instrument, criteria, clinician or process for either group, no IQ or severity measure, and a 17-point sex imbalance between groups that is never tested or discussed." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.97"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "To handle any such missing data and consistently estimate the SampEn, we selected the segment in m+1 dimension only if the respective vector was embedded with no missing data. ... Instead, if we would have just concatenated the data points, the template 16 or 17 (without considering the missing value) would have matched with 25 and 26, thereby (artificially) increasing Cm without necessarily increasing Cm+1, or vice versa, leading to inaccurate results." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:665e8c7a855d> ;
            slr:claim_label "Missing data are handled inside the entropy computation with a stated rule and worked example, rather than by interpolation or concatenation - the most careful missing-data treatment in this corpus, and necessary because toddlers move." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the feature related to the image center was only selected by the ASD group patients. These findings are in agreement with the results found by Wang et al., who realized that the ASD group had a greater focus on the center of the image, even when there was nothing in the center." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-021-89023-8> ;
            slr:claim_label "Distance to the image centre was retained only in the autistic group's attention model, consistent with prior reports of centre fixation in autism." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The ANN reached accuracy, precision, sensitivity, specificity, and AUC of 100% for all measures during the training and validated phases. Meanwhile, the accuracy, precision, sensitivity, specificity and AUC achieved during the testing phase were 98.7%, 100%, 100%, 98.2% and 99.77%, respectively. The overall accuracy of the ANN classifier was 99.8%." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/electronics11040530> ;
            slr:claim_label "The headline 99.8% pools training, validation and testing performance; the held-out test figure for the same model is 98.7%." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
