            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "future research will have to evaluate intellectual disability, which is an important source of inter-subject variability in ASD that seems to impact motor planning and coordination... The inclusion of additional diagnostic classes (e.g. developmental coordination disorder, attention deficit with hyperactivity disorders) would facilitate a dimensional acknowledgment of atypical development" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cognition.2021.104652> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors identify absent cognitive measurement and absent other-diagnosis comparison groups as the principal next steps." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In these experiments, no data from the participants from the test set was used for training (i.e. the test and training sets were divided on the basis of participants). This is not the case with the EEG study where the authors used 10-fold cross-validation where \"the data is randomly partitioned, into 10 subsets with the same size and with the same number of EEG segments\". Dividing the training and tests sets in this way makes it possible for different data segments from the same participant to be used for training and testing, allowing for higher accuracy owing to similarity between the data in the two sets." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1145/3192714.3192819> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors identify segment-level rather than participant-level partitioning in prior autism classification studies as a source of inflated accuracy." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The three classifiers attained similar overall performance, indicating that the simpler machine learning methods suffice for the given dataset." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1145/3371382.3378382> ;
            slr:claim_label "CNN, random forest and k-nearest neighbour performed equivalently, which the authors interpret as simpler methods sufficing at this data scale." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Since STAR-FC is trained on general population, it is assumed that it models the scan path of TD subjects." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:10ab04b596b1> ;
            slr:claim_label "A computational saccade generator trained on the general population serves as a synthetic typically developing baseline against which real scanpaths are compared." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
