            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-65384-4> ;
            slr:claim_label "Nested validation with independent-sample testing produced accuracies of 73% kinematic, 70% eye movement and 78% combined." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "K-ADOS-2 CSS Mean (SD) 6.07 (1.6) ... SA CSS 6.62 (1.8) ... RRB CSS 6.16 (2.2) ... K-ADOS-2 module, No. (%) T 8 (17.8) / 1 28 (62.2) / 2 9 (20.0)" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:6131bfb6ef7c> ;
            slr:claim_label "Calibrated severity scores across three domains and module distribution are reported, establishing that the autistic sample is predominantly preverbal or single-word - a population systematically excluded by paradigms requiring screen attention or conversation, and one this study uniquely addresses." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.91"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Currently, there is no available public speech dataset for ASD children, which creates a big obstacle for related research." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:ceb7a2194e61> ;
            slr:claim_label "The absence of shared paediatric autism speech corpora is identified as a field-level obstacle, and this study's own corpus of roughly 7,000 recordings is not released." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Therefore, we followed the basic idea in [35] to assign labels of 1 to all the test visual stimuli of the ASD group and 0 to those of the TD group." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:5e6c6c482e7c> ;
