        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "If the patient is facing the front of the robot body, where the mobile phone is attached, the face of the patient is detected, therefore it is assumed that he or she is paying attention to the robot. Thus, the assessment system increments the attention score by 5 points. If the face of the patient is not facing the robot ... decrements the attention score by 1 point. The operator can change the preset increment and decrement values so that each patient has individual settings." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s12369-020-00639-8> ;
            slr:claim_label "Fully transparent rule-based scoring with operator-adjustable constants - readable and tunable by the clinician using it, and the opposite design point from the learned models elsewhere in this review. It also equates a detected face with attending, and makes scores non-comparable across children." ;
