            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "First, note that pose-pose features (i.e., features that summarize correlation between two head rotation angles) have the greatest weight on average, indicating that head movements are important for distinguishing behavioral patterns of autistic vs NT participants. ... while the baseline rate of pose features is only ~5.3% ... the top 10 features contain a pose-related feature at a ratio of ~13.3%." ] ;
