            slr:relevance_score "0.91"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "There were 2 adults with ASD, 1 adult with Sz, an adult in the control group, and 4 children with ASD and one control child who could not be detected correctly by any of the 4 models constructed in this study. We checked the data for these individuals and noted that their gaze did not move from the center at all. Considering the possibility that they were not solving the task seriously, we checked the FEIT scores and found that their scores were not lower. ... This suggests that people with wide peripheral vision may be able to successfully complete the task without moving their eyes." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fdgth.2023.952433> ;
            slr:claim_label "An individual-level error analysis identifying a failure mode intrinsic to gaze-based assessment - participants who complete the task by peripheral vision without moving their eyes, undetectable as non-compliant because their recognition scores are normal, affecting 6.5% of adults and 17% of children." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.98"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "For each participant, the diagnosis was determined according to DSM-5 research criteria for schizophrenia or ASD. The ASDs were re-evaluated using the Autism Disorder Observation Schedule-2nd Ed. The Szs were re-evaluated using the positive and negative syndrome scale for schizotypy symptoms. ... No controls had lerning delays and communication problems because physicians and psychologists interviewed them and excluded." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fdgth.2023.952433> ;
            slr:claim_label "DSM-5 criteria with condition-specific instrument re-evaluation for both clinical groups, and controls actively screened by clinicians rather than assumed - among the strongest reference-standard configurations in this review." ;
