        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Assessment is typically performed at the time of enrollment and repeated during long-term therapy to measure progress. If assessments could be repeated more frequently to trace the severity and development of symptoms, then therapists could implement more efficacious diagnostic and therapeutic options, and patients and their parents would be better motivated to withstand long, repetitive therapy sessions." ] ;
