        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Since the size of the training set is small compared to the size of the feature vector, feature reduction is necessary before applying machine learning methods. Addressing the mentioned problem, we applied two consecutive backward eliminations on all the features. ... The best result was obtained by integrating seven acceleration features and three shaft encoder features." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/su15107790> ;
            slr:claim_label "Two rounds of backward elimination reduced 54 features to 10 on the whole sample, with no statement of nesting inside the cross-validation folds - the regime in which selection bias is largest." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "an additional node hosted in the most powerful workstation carries out a data fusion of all navigation messages that were generated in the local processing stage. In addition to the fusion, this node computes the visual focus of attention (VFOA) and publishes this as a std msgs/Header, in which the time stamp and the target name of the VFOA estimation are registered." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10846-018-00975-y> ;
            slr:claim_label "The most developed measurement infrastructure in the review: distributed per-camera face analysis with asynchronous cross-camera fusion producing a timestamped, semantically labelled attention target - a direct answer to the occlusion problem in single-camera gaze measurement." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.94"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
