        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "This study shared the same dataset as our previous research [28], which reported excessive and less complex whole-body movement in children with ASD, yet failed to find significant differences in IMC between the ASD and TD children. The previous research used complexity matching as the analytic technique... Differently, the present study implemented cross wavelet analysis (CWA) to quantify IMC at different movement frequencies." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:12accba36eb4> ;
            slr:claim_label "The same recordings analysed by the same group with a different technique moved from no significant coordination difference to a significant one plus a 92.68% classifier - the review's clearest demonstration of how much analytic choice determines the reported outcome." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.99"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Though the datasets are relatively imbalanced, this study did not consider any category to be grossly imbalanced. Hence, oversampling was not applied to the training sets for all categories before modelling." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:74a48b2cecd0> ;
            slr:claim_label "A deliberate and explained decision not to oversample, which avoids the synthetic-minority inflation affecting several comparators in the paper's own literature review - an example of the analytic care that surrounds the corrupted target." ;
