            slr:relevance_score "0.91"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Each participant's video was segmented into individual frames using Python, from which 50 frames were selected out of an initial 500 frames. For each selected frame, both the left and right eye images were extracted, resulting in 100 images per participant (50 frames x 2 eyes). Consequently, each severity category comprised 1000 images, amounting to a dataset of 4000 images in total. In order to provide reliable model training and evaluation... this dataset was divided into training, testing, and validation subsets in an 70:15:15 ratio." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:420caf43bd93> ;
            slr:claim_label "The split is at the eye-image level with a fixed 100 images per child, so all 40 participants necessarily appear in the training, validation and test subsets simultaneously." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.99"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
