            slr:relevance_score "0.86"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In the diagnosis task (TD, ASD, DYS, NOS), D-FT also demonstrated superior performance (60.9% UAR) compared to W2V2-FT (54.3%). These results highlight the potential of transfer learning for speech-based ASD recognition and underscore the challenges of multi-class classification with limited labeled data." ] ;
