            slr:claim_label "A four-class task separating autism from dysphasia and PDD-NOS - one of only two studies in the review with non-autistic clinical comparison groups - and the resulting 60.9% against a 25% chance level is the most informative number in the paper." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.94"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "as the AOIs are correlated, the Bonferroni correction is extremely stringent and will reduce the likelihood of Type 1 errors." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:b694f7dc9504> ;
            slr:claim_label "The conservatism of the correction is acknowledged explicitly, making the two surviving findings more credible." ;
