        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "+e powers of the ﬁve frequency bands in an eﬀective epoch were extracted, and a t-test was run to explore the diﬀerences in EEG in various brain regions of the two groups under distinct frequency bands. ... in this study, the power of diﬀerent brain regions with signiﬁcant diﬀerences was extracted as EEG features to distinguish ASD in TD children." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:71950da5db46> ;
            slr:claim_label "EEG features were selected by significance testing across the whole sample, so held-out labels informed feature selection before cross-validation." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.98"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "An in-depth investigation into the top-selected features showed that for the PNN classifier the means of H*1 -A*3 and H4, the standard deviation of H1, and the range of F0 and shimmer parameters obtained high importance." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:3c2b7ea0e8c0> ;
            slr:claim_label "Vocal-quality measures and F0 range were the most informative features for the PNN." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "usingonlythetwoleastsignificantfeaturesAgeandsex,resultinginasensitivityof99.5%. Subsequently,theattributesQ1-Q10wereaddedoneatatime... WhenonlyQ1wasadded,thesensitivitywas97.6%.However,asQ2andQ3wereadded,sensitivitydroppedto92.8%" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1088/2631-8695/addb0b> ;
            slr:claim_label "Age and sex alone give 99.5% sensitivity on a dataset that is 69.1% positive - the signature of a near-all-positive classifier - and the surrounding text reads subsequent declines as degradation rather than as evidence that sensitivity alone is uninformative here." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.98"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Studies have utilised pre-trained CNNs like VGG16, VGG19, and EfficientNetB0... However, these models face challenges such as high computational costs and limited generalizability across diverse demographics [1]... yet cross-validation may not reflect real-world variability, risking overfitting [3]" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.22266/ijies2025.0430.21> ;
            slr:claim_label "A specific limitation is attached to roughly twenty prior studies, including overfitting risk in validation design, while no limitation is stated for this study's own single unrepeated split." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.91"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Participants were not informed of the function of the eye tracker, and they were asked to avoid moving the glasses... A postexperiment interview confirmed that none of the participants was aware that their gaze behavior had been recorded." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.2196/29328> ;
            slr:claim_label "Participants were unaware their gaze was being recorded, verified by post-experiment interview, so gaze behaviour was not self-conscious." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We rotated each image in the original dataset by 45, 60, 90, and 180 degrees, resulting in a synthetic dataset of 2566 RGB images consisting of 1047 ASD and 1519 TDs." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics12020518> ;
            slr:claim_label "Augmentation was applied to the whole dataset before partitioning, and rotation by 45 and 60 degrees produces physically impossible gaze trajectories." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The study was approved by the autism specialist and director board of ARC. The recruited participants were also evaluated clinically based on Childhood Autism Rating Scale Schedule (CARS) by the autism experts. Parents have also signed the consent form" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1177/07356331211040405> ;
            slr:claim_label "Governance rests on centre-level approval and parental consent, with CARS supplying both eligibility and the reference severity categories." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "This study has utilized a freely accessible dataset comprising 547 eye-tracking systems that can be used to scan pathways obtained from 328 characteristically emerging children and 219 children with autism." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:bb59da535587> ;
            slr:claim_label "The abstract reports image counts as child counts, inflating the apparent cohort from a few dozen children to 547." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.96"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Although ResNet18 structure has a deeper level, it cannot achieve better diagnosis performance from the experiment. The possible reason is that simply and rudely cascading EEG and eye-tracking recordings cannot make good use of multi-modality information." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2021.651349> ;
            slr:claim_label "A deeper network over concatenated features performed worst of all comparators, supporting the claim that the fusion mechanism rather than model capacity determines performance." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the interpretation of our method is constrained by the prevalence of the ASD in the general population (around 1%), which is much lower than the rate of ASD in our sample (33%)" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:752eeff1ddb3> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors explicitly caveat that sample prevalence (33%) far exceeds population prevalence (~1%), limiting the practical predictive value." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "A total of 23 classifiers were evaluated from the different types of classifiers available... The proposed model records its best performances when the TreeBagger classifier is used." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:5908df2cffca> ;
