        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "a pseudo group was created, which contained 21 pairs of time series. Each pair of time series was composed of one time series of a child in one video and one time series of the adult from a different video. Since no actual interaction occurred between the child and the adult in the pseudo group, the level of IMC could be regarded as representing interaction at the chance level." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:12accba36eb4> ;
            slr:claim_label "A genuine empirical chance level for a synchrony measure, constructed by breaking the dyad - the best chance-level control in this review, and what allows the finding to be stated as reduced real coordination rather than an unspecified difference." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.96"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "TABLE II. Confusion matrix for CNN model ... Non-ASD (0) 30 4 / ASD (1) 12 11 ... TABLE III. Class 0 Precision 0.71 Recall 0.88 F1 0.79 / Class 1 Precision 0.73 Recall 0.48 F1 0.58" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:ff89c89464cc> ;
            slr:claim_label "The custom CNN's reported 71.9% accuracy conceals autism-class recall of 0.48 - fewer than half the autism images detected, below the 59.6% majority-class baseline implied by the same matrix - visible only because per-class metrics and the confusion matrix were published." ;
