            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:363f034a75b7> ;
            slr:claim_label "The pose-based classifier reached 72.4% accuracy with 0.72 precision and 0.92 recall." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We also removed any hashtags or a list of keywords related to autism such as “actuallyautistic,” “autism,” “autistic,” ... and “autismspeaks,” which could introduce bias and lead to model overfitting." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:b4ca4bcef771> ;
            slr:claim_label "A deliberate target-leakage control: since the label is defined by hashtag use, leaving these tokens in would make the task a lookup of the label. This is the same failure this review documents in the questionnaire-item studies, addressed here rather than ignored." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.96"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "autism spectrum disorder, motor biomarkers, random forest, SHAP analysis, violence level classification" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2026.1751654> ;
            slr:claim_label "A keyword from an unrelated manuscript (violence level classification) survives in the published article." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.75"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The study utilised MRI datasets of newborns comprising 10,000 samples... The final dataset included 25,000 positive cases and 1200 negative cases, with class balance maintained." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:2062d0824ac5> ;
            slr:claim_label "The sample description is arithmetically impossible - 25,000 positives from 10,000 samples - and a 21-to-1 class ratio is described as balanced." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.99"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Thus, analyses of the Creativity gameplay by RGF2 analysis produced the best predictive scores with an area under the Receiver-Operator Characteristics curve (AUC) of up to 0.93 (Fig. 3) and sensitivity and specificity up to, for example, 83% with 85% specificity (Table 2)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/srep31107> ;
            slr:claim_label "The best model reached AUC 0.93 with 83% sensitivity at 85% specificity on the free-play Creativity game." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In our study, K was set to 8, 12, 16, and 20, and we divided diﬀerent AOIs by using the K-means algorithm... +e ﬁnal value of K was determined from the experimental results." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:71950da5db46> ;
            slr:claim_label "The gaze preprocessing hyperparameter was chosen on the basis of classification results across the full sample." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The children were admitted into this clinic based on the diagnosis made by a pediatric psychiatrist and a pediatric clinical psychologist and underwent a comprehensive evaluation." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s11760-023-02668-y> ;
            slr:claim_label "The reference standard is clinic admission following two-clinician diagnosis, with no instrument, criteria version, date or reliability reported, and no screening at all for the school-recruited comparison group." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.88"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Importantly, our model was similarly accurate for classifying ASD (66%) compared with human raters (67%). However, human raters outperformed our system in classifying TD children." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:80626146cad2> ;
            slr:claim_label "The model matched human raters on identifying autistic children but was outperformed on identifying typically developing children." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We speculate that the presence of greater predictability with minor facial movements in the TD toddlers reflects a higher level and more consistent understanding of the shared social meaning of content of the movies (e.g., rhymes, a conversation). If so, the TD toddlers might be expected to respond more predictably to the stimuli, whereas the responses of the children with autism may be more idiosyncratic." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:665e8c7a855d> ;
            slr:claim_label "The substantive interpretation is labelled as speculation and framed in terms of idiosyncrasy rather than deficit - a notably measured register for this literature." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.84"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Interestingly, older participants in both groups were more often labeled as autistic than young participants by the machine-learning classifiers, as the classifier was probably picking up a tendency of higher age in the ASD group. This age bias points to the strong need of careful testing for confounders and biases in training data for all kind of machine-learning diagnostic methods." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41746-020-0227-5> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors identify an age bias in their own classifier arising from unmatched groups and generalise it as a warning about confounders in training data." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "This allows clinicians to directly visualize how an increase in, say, ADOS-Gotham_Total or ADI_R_RRB_Total_C, elevates the predicted ASD probability." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics15172232> ;
            slr:claim_label "The paper states its own circularity as a feature: the model's predicted autism probability rises with the score on the instrument used to diagnose autism. Presented as clinical alignment, it is target leakage described in the authors' own words." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.99"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Unlike visible image-based methods, thermal imaging is not affected by lighting conditions or skin tone, making it an advantageous tool for behavioral analysis." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:c846224c5959> ;
            slr:claim_label "A sensor-level answer to the demographic and photographic fragility that undermines the visible-spectrum facial studies charted elsewhere in this review - the best-argued modality choice in the corpus, undone by the evaluation it supports." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Notwithstanding the fact that in addition to the complexity measure it would be necessary to combine other features such as gaze-related indices, name call response, signatures of motor deficits, and more, as mentioned in [7], before deploying such automated decision-making tool." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:665e8c7a855d> ;
            slr:claim_label "The translational claim is explicitly conditional: the biomarker is proposed as one component of a multi-signal tool, with combination stated as a precondition of deployment rather than an aspiration." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Dropout: 0.5 1.0000 0.7440 0.6828 | Dropout: 0.2 1.0000 0.7440 0.6699 | CNN Dropout: 0.5 0.9784 0.7249 0.7207" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1145/3539226> ;
            slr:claim_label "Training accuracy reaches 100% while test accuracy sits at 74% - a pattern repeated in essentially every one of fourteen tables, indicating complete memorisation at every hyperparameter setting tried. Reporting training accuracy makes this visible, which most studies in this corpus do not." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.94"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "if we compare the recall of the models in the preliminary experiment and the models in the test experiment, we notice that some models which show high recall in the preliminary experiment, like GBDT, now have poor performance in the test experiment. Rather, the recall of models like Naïve Bayes, significantly increases. This indicates that the data patterns of the adults we recruited in the preliminary experiment are somehow different from those autistic adults." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1111/jcap.12346> ;
            slr:claim_label "Individual model recall shifted markedly between experiments, which the authors interpret as showing the two populations have different data patterns." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the experimental validation analysis of the EDLM-ASDDFI algorithm is examined using the Autism image dataset, which comprises 2926 facial samples with two classes (Normal and Autism)" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.32604/cmc.2025.062266> ;
            slr:claim_label "The analysis unit is the image from a public Kaggle corpus; no participant, demographic or diagnostic information exists." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.93"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The age of children with ASD lied in the range from 5 to 12 years old (8 years old on average). 300 different images were used in the experiment. Each image was viewed by 14 ASD children and 14 TD children. Each child viewed one image with the original full resolution for 3 s. The scan-path data was collected by Tobii T120 eye tracker with a 17-inch monitor." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:e51e9878eb2c> ;
            slr:claim_label "Age is reported for the autistic group only; no demographic information is given for the comparison group." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Moreover, we used the fitted distribution instead of the predictor network, to prevent the predictor from incorrect classification, i.e., new participants being mapped in unknown zones of the latent space. Indeed, restricting the analysis to the latent distributions reduces the probability of misclassifying new inputs." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:06efef346587> ;
            slr:claim_label "A deliberate out-of-distribution safeguard: classification by fitted class-conditional density rather than by the trained predictor, so a participant landing in an unvisited latent region is treated conservatively - the most careful handling of novel inputs in this corpus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Rigorous data-preprocessing improved the models' generalizability and real-world applicability across diverse clinical datasets, ensuring a robust performance." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:2acd51f637a5> ;
            slr:claim_label "Applicability across diverse clinical datasets is claimed from a single dataset with no external cohort." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The experimental data comes from the process of clinical screening for ASD, which has less laboratory control, more realistic child response, and a flexible number of accompanying parents." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:3dafd8b400d2> ;
            slr:claim_label "Recording inside live ADOS-2 assessments with the protocol unmodified and parental presence unconstrained - a deliberate choice of the deployment distribution over laboratory control, and the engineering reason multi-object tracking is required." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.89"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Three coders, with prior experience ranging from 3 months to 11 years in medical training or ASD intervention, participated in this study ... To evaluate inter-coder consistency, the three coders coded the same sample of 30 children independently. Results showed that their consistency reached 83.7-91.7%." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s12888-024-06129-9> ;
            slr:claim_label "Measurement reliability quantified rather than assumed, on a shared subsample, with the formula given - the analogue of a calibration procedure for a human-coded study, and absent from most observational work in this review." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Moreover, the classifier should include conditions overlapping with autism for differential diagnosis." ] ;
