            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Studies using EEG and speech data report results from 10-fold cross validation instead of LOOCV, where the accuracy is 94% for EEG data [11] and 93% for speech data [12]. These are potentially overoptimistic as different data segments from the same participant are assigned to the training and testing sets, thus increasing the similarity between the two. In other words, this evaluation set-up does not correspond to real-world applications where the system has to categorize a user, portions of whose data are not included in the training set." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/TNSRE.2020.2991675> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors identify segment-level rather than participant-level splitting as the reason prior EEG and speech accuracies of 93-94% are likely overoptimistic." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "IQ was assessed for the entire sample using the Leiter-3 International Performance Scale. The IQ score for the TD group ranged between 74 and 110, while the ASD group covered a range from 59 to 109. Six children in the ASD group had mild mental retardation with an IQ score between 59 and 70." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:06efef346587> ;
            slr:claim_label "IQ is reported only as ranges with no means, SDs or comparison, and six autistic children fall below the comparison group's floor - an uncontrolled asymmetry in a study whose task is a cognitive test." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.88"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "This method uses a number of convolutional layers to find important patterns in the image, such as the shape of the face, the expression on it, and the texture of the skin." ] ;
