        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "EEG had the advantage of classifying ASD (90.00%) compared with eye ﬁxation (62.50%) and facial expression (72.50%), facial expression outperformed EEG in recognizing TD (92.50% versus 77.50%)... Eye ﬁxation misclassiﬁed more ASDs as TDs (37.50%), whereas EEG misclassiﬁed more TDs as ASDs (22.50%)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:71950da5db46> ;
            slr:claim_label "The three modalities fail in systematically opposite directions across classes, which is the demonstrated mechanism of the fusion gain." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "This study achieved an accuracy of 96%, but employed a lower sample size (N = 30), Support Vector Machine approach, and a leave-one-out cross-validation that altogether render this methodology prone to over-fitting. In our study, we worked to reduce over-fitting with larger subject numbers (N = 82), a Regularized Greedy Forest approach, and 10 repetitions of a 10-fold cross-validation procedure." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/srep31107> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors explicitly criticise the prior SVM-plus-leave-one-out motor classification study as overfitting-prone and adopt repeated cross-validation with regularised ensembles instead." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The diagnosis was made by a neuropsychiatrist according to DSM-5 criteria." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:602daaeb6643> ;
            slr:claim_label "Diagnostic ascertainment is described in a single clause with no instrument, procedure or severity measure." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Horizontal Flip: Mirrors the image around a vertical line running through its center." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:3dc286a9aa92> ;
            slr:claim_label "Augmentation includes horizontal flipping, which generates mirrored scanpaths that no viewer could have produced on the original stimulus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The choice of the reduced dimensionality (2D estimated postural representations) in input videos was two-fold: to allow a pure focus on non-verbal interaction patterns and ensure de-identification of the persons involved (skeletal points plotted against the black background)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-021-94378-z> ;
            slr:claim_label "De-identification and confound removal are achieved by the same representational choice." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Data analysis for this project is constantly independently reviewed by Scott Compton, who has no conflict of interest related to this work. Sapiro, Dawson, Carpenter, and Espinosa developed technology related to the app that has been licensed to Apple, Inc., and both they and Duke University have benefited financially." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:665e8c7a855d> ;
            slr:claim_label "The most detailed competing-interests disclosure in this corpus, paired with a structural mitigation - continuous independent analysis review by a named conflict-free co-author - that no other study here reports." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.87"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Using the Vicon motion tracking system, gait data were collected from 21 subjects, 12 of these subjects clinically diagnosed as having ASD, while the remaining 9 were typically developed (TD)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:51915c87b5e5> ;
            slr:claim_label "The entire participant description is 12 clinically diagnosed autistic and 9 typically developed subjects, with no demographic or diagnostic detail." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The authors (Z.M., Y.J., JH.C., Y.G., X.L., and J.L.) declare that there were two patent applications related to this research (No. 202310300588.1 and No. 202310315701.3)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1186/s12888-024-06129-9> ;
            slr:claim_label "Patent applications arising from the coding scheme and prediction model are declared at the level of individual authors, alongside a commercial autism-services affiliation for four of them - relevant context for a paper proposing the tool for clinical deployment." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.82"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Individuals with ASD and those who disclosed a history of experiencing a stroke were shown to use a considerably higher number of unique words during their experience with FreeSpeech." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:0ce05e9cde34> ;
            slr:claim_label "Lexical content is recoverable and group-discriminating in the descriptive analysis, yet the classification pipeline discards it entirely by reducing every key press to a category-preserving integer - an unexplained choice, and a plausible unmeasured proxy for expressive language level." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.88"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The SVM classiﬁer had an average accuracy of 0.739. Speciﬁcally, accuracy resulted larger than 0.7 in 15 children; between 0.6 and 0.7 in 6 children; lower than 0.6 in the remaining 5 children. The ROC curve had an AUC of 0.947, with a sensitivity of 0.846 and a speciﬁcity of 0.923 at its optimal operating point" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cognition.2021.104652> ;
            slr:claim_label "Trial-level accuracy was 0.739 with five of 26 children below 0.6, while the subject-level AUC was 0.947." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In the first study (Simeoli et al., 2020), by using descriptive analysis, we observed some specificity of the ASD motion pattern. Results revealed that ASD trajectories were characterised by low linearity, high MaxSpeed and MaxAcceleration values, and low MinumumSpeed and MinimumAcceleration values. However, it was impossible to distinguish significant differences between the two groups." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:06efef346587> ;
            slr:claim_label "Conventional descriptive statistics on the same data failed to separate the groups significantly; the reported separation emerges only under the deep model, which raises the question of what the model is separating - and the speed direction partly reverses between the two analyses." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.94"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "LMEMs showed that ASD children had signiﬁcantly greater RR and ARPM in all the pitch, yaw, and roll directions as compared to the TD group, with all p-values lower than 0.05." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10803-021-05179-2> ;
            slr:claim_label "Rotation range and amount of rotation per minute were significantly greater in autistic children in all three rotational axes." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "we only identified IJA towards the therapist in the transition between mediators, for ASD children. This fact shows a clear difference of behavior pattern between CwASD and TD children, which can be analyzed using a JA task protocol." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10846-018-00975-y> ;
            slr:claim_label "A subtype-specific, partner-specific behavioural claim - but from three children per group with no statistical test, and confounded by a mediator order that was never counterbalanced." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the dataset—sourced from publicly available 2D facial images—may not fully represent the diversity of facial expressions in children with ASD or gelotophobia, as demographic variables, such as age, gender, and cultural background, were not explicitly controlled" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:35c8bd7a6e13> ;
            slr:claim_label "Uncontrolled demographics named directly by the authors - creditable candour, and material given that the feature extractor is optimised to encode facial identity and therefore represents demographic attributes strongly." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The internal model parameters for SVM and ANN classifiers were optimized using exhaustive grid search strategy." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:b7546602bf4b> ;
            slr:claim_label "Model hyperparameters were selected by exhaustive grid search, described outside the cross-validation procedure." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The dataset is composed of 80 children with ASD (2.68 ± 0.89 years old; 48 males, 32 females) as well as 80 typically developing (TD) children matched for age (2.46 ± 0.98 years old) and gender (48 males, 32 females)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:dac3e7a03f26> ;
            slr:claim_label "Exact sex matching at 40% female in both groups - the highest female representation in the review and the only instance of deliberate exact matching, in a corpus where a sex-stratified analysis elsewhere revealed a fifty-point sensitivity gap." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Notwithstanding, further work is still needed to investigate if the obtained results will remain once toddlers with other non ASD-related language development disorders are included in the analysis." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:3c2b7ea0e8c0> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors flag untested specificity against other language development disorders as the key open question." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The system successfully diagnosed ASD using the ET dataset. This approach shows promise for clinical application, assisting healthcare professionals in diagnosing ASD more accurately through advanced artificial intelligence technology." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:272c3ab22999> ;
            slr:claim_label "An unqualified clinical-deployment claim is made from a leakage-affected, sample-level result with no limitations section and no ethics statement." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "This study demonstrates the effectiveness of combining deep learning techniques with validated diagnostic tools for detecting gelotophobia, particularly in individuals with ASD." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:35c8bd7a6e13> ;
            slr:claim_label "Effectiveness for the paper's headline target is asserted although no gelotophobia measurement was made on any person and no metric for that task appears anywhere - the only primary claim in this review resting on no measurement at all." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.98"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The collection presently comprises 547 images... More precisely, there were 328 images for the people without ASD, and 219 images for the persons diagnosed with ASD." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:bb59da535587> ;
            slr:claim_label "The methods give the correct reading - these are image counts from a scanpath collection with multiple images per child - contradicting the abstract." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.94"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In the context of this study, majority class prediction requires every participant sample to be predicted as \"TD\". Thus, the classification accuracy of majority class prediction would be 51.3% (ie, 20/39), which is greatly lower than the optimal classification accuracy of our results." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.2196/29328> ;
            slr:claim_label "A majority-class baseline of 51.3% was computed and compared against the reported accuracy." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The dataset was augmented with additional 2,735 samples, where five synthetic images were generated for each visualization." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:2bf712f2292c> ;
            slr:claim_label "Fivefold augmentation produced 2,735 synthetic images derived from the original 547 before model training." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Participants were neither told the genuine function of the eye tracker, nor suggested to move the glasses or to make abrupt or intense head movements. Post-experiment questions asked whether they knew the genuine function of the glasses, and none of them were aware that the eye tracker was used for recording gaze behavior." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10803-022-05685-x> ;
            slr:claim_label "A documented control against reactive gaze behaviour, verified by post-experiment questioning - a methodological safeguard rarely reported in this corpus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.8"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The classification performance with different number of feature(s) for the 9-s behavior segments is presented in Table 3, which shows that the maximum classification accuracy was yielded with only one feature - entropy in the x-y coordinate plane." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10803-022-05685-x> ;
            slr:claim_label "A single interpretable feature - the entropy of spatial gaze allocation - carries the whole segment-level signal, with additional features slightly degrading accuracy." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.86"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Considering the collinearity between our ADOS measures we employed the Partial Least Squares Correlation (PLS-C) analysis... we performed the permutation testing by generating 1000 permutation samples... The stability of the obtained saliences U and V is obtained by creating 1000 bootstrap samples" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-021-94378-z> ;
            slr:claim_label "Collinearity among symptom items was handled by a permutation-tested, bootstrap-stabilised multivariate analysis rather than by repeated univariate tests." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Similarly, we need to compare imitation in ASC with other groups that are known to have motor deficits such as Developmental Coordination Disorder and Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:8da61cddafb9> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors identify comparison against other motor-deficit conditions as necessary to establish autism specificity." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The dataset comprised 100 children, aged 5–9 years (50 with ASD, 50 typically developing (TD))." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.11591/eei.v14i5.10319> ;
            slr:claim_label "The only participant description offered: no recruitment source, no diagnostic instrument, criteria or clinician, no age distribution by group, and no cognitive or language characterisation, in a prospectively recruited sample." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.93"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Due to a limited access to established ASD diagnostic instruments such as ADOS and ADI-R, the accuracy of the ASD diagnosis in the present study was assured through a variety of other rigorous procedures. Specifically, by strictly following the DSM-IV criteria, the diagnosis of ASD was first made by a licensed psychiatrist with no less than five years' clinical experience, and then the diagnosis was further evaluated by a senior psychiatrist. Additional consultation with at least two other senior psychiatrists would be conducted if disagreement between psychiatrists took place." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10803-022-05685-x> ;
            slr:claim_label "The reference standard is a multi-psychiatrist DSM-IV consensus rather than a standardised instrument, disclosed transparently along with the reason." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.94"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In order to limit over-fitting to the idiosyncratic characteristics of our participants, we performed leave-one-subject-out cross validation when evaluating SVM performance... This form of cross validation is recommended by Saeb et al. (2017), due to its approximation of the clinically relevant use-case of diagnosis in unseen participants." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1002/aur.2733> ;
            slr:claim_label "Subject-wise cross-validation was adopted with explicit citation to the methodological literature on record-wise versus subject-wise validation." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Ana Laguna and Sandra Pusil are employed by Zoundream AG. Ana Laguna is also co-founder of the company and owns stock in Zoundream AG. Silvia Orlandi received compensation for the collaboration as members of the scientific advisory board of Zoundream AG." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10803-025-06811-1> ;
            slr:claim_label "The fullest competing-interest declaration in the review, itemising employment, founder status, equity holding and advisory compensation by individual alongside company funding of the research - the standard other commercially sponsored studies here should meet." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.92"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Two experienced transcribers independently transcribed the narrative produced by a participant, with word-level reliability averaging 91%. The transcribers were blind for diagnosis" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1111/1460-6984.12731> ;
            slr:claim_label "Transcription reliability was quantified between independent blind transcribers - the only such figure in the corpus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Training and evaluation were carried out multiple times and results were highly consistent across all the runs, indicating that stable behaviour of the model." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.47310/jpms2026150119> ;
            slr:claim_label "Repeated-run consistency is asserted with no variance figure reported." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.84"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the model predicts a score within +/-5 % of the true value for 36.3.% of cases. When the tolerance increased to 10 %, the percentage of cases would increase above 60 %." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:58f57df91746> ;
            slr:claim_label "An individual-level tolerance analysis states plainly what R=.85 delivers per person - a form of reporting absent everywhere else in the corpus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.94"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In the training set this imbalance was addressed by upsampling the minority class, to enable learning better representation of this class. Whilst the development and test sets remain intact with their distributions unchanged, to be representative of real-world." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fdgth.2025.1274675> ;
            slr:claim_label "Rebalancing confined to training with evaluation distributions deliberately preserved - a correct and explicitly reasoned choice that very few papers in this corpus make, and one whose absence elsewhere is a silent source of inflation." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "It is also noteworthy that ROIs that encompass the eyes proved to be more capable of distinguishing individuals from the two groups than ROIs that consider the therapist's hand." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/CBMS52027.2021.00016> ;
            slr:claim_label "Regions containing the eyes were more discriminative than regions containing the pointing hand." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We observe that relying on any single data source leads to a substantially lower F1-score compared to the joint analysis approach. This proves the effectiveness of the proposed multi-source joint analysis." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1145/3233547.3233574> ;
            slr:claim_label "Every single data source performed substantially worse alone than the fused multi-source model." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "For each input combination we only report the results of the best performing classifier." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1111/1460-6984.12731> ;
            slr:claim_label "Each reported figure is the maximum over at least three classifier families, selected on the same leave-one-out folds used for reporting." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "We worked in conjunction with the FDA to establish minimum thresholds for PPV and NPV, which were the primary endpoints for this pivotal study. Once established, we used these values (PPV greater than 65% and NPV greater than 85%) as the boundaries to govern the model's range of acceptable outcomes during model hyperparameter tuning." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41746-022-00598-6> ;
            slr:claim_label "Endpoints and abstention thresholds were pre-specified with the regulator and fixed on prior data before the trial, making this an external validation of a locked model." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Participants, primarily college students (N = 54), who were recruited and assessed as non-AS, indicative of not exhibiting AS characteristics according to the ADOS-2 assessment by a research reliability-established administrator. ... While IQ testing was not part of our methodology, we selected individuals with a GPA range of 2.4 to 2.8, a range statistically representative of the average for Japanese college students" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:e15a1551c489> ;
            slr:claim_label "Every comparison participant was ADOS-2-screened and confirmed non-spectrum - the strongest comparison-group screening in the review - but cognitive ability was not measured, with college grade point average substituted, leaving an unquantified ability gap against an autistic group whose full-scale IQ is 81-91." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.98"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "we first selected features significantly correlated with the diagnostic status of the training set (p < 0.025) using univariate Pearson correlation within each cross-validation fold. ... we further implemented Principal Component Analysis for feature reduction and used the first 10 components for model training." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:80626146cad2> ;
            slr:claim_label "Feature selection and dimensionality reduction were performed within each cross-validation fold rather than on the full dataset." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "SVM 59.71% 61.09% 60.84% 59.23% / CNN 55.19% 55.74% 62.94% 59.13%" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:ceb7a2194e61> ;
            slr:claim_label "The separated frequency-domain outputs classify near chance, which is difficult to reconcile with the near-perfect performance of the unmixing matrix that produced that separation." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "we used the Maximum Between-Class Variance method to select the threshold for binarizing the scores of all pieces in both training and testing" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1145/3440067.3440078> ;
            slr:claim_label "The classification threshold is computed by Otsu maximum between-class variance on the score distribution being classified, including at test time." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the average accuracy rates of Net Dwell Time based classification were 70,67% and 79,17%... our average accuracy rates in ML based classification with a selected set of features were 78,12% and 84,37%" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:533b421d2f0b> ;
            slr:claim_label "A single-feature ablation shows the multivariate feature set outperforms the best individual metric." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Even missing out certain pages may provide clues to identify ASD participants. Reflecting such phenomena is indeed the best in the case of combined pages and 0s utterance representation" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1111/1460-6984.12731> ;
            slr:claim_label "Zero-vector representation outperformed masking, supporting the interpretation that pages a participant skipped carry signal rather than being missing data." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "we can state that the model is not more trustable after a threshold of 0.9 where the detection accuracy over full data scores under the random chance." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:34584d91747b> ;
            slr:claim_label "A confidence-threshold sensitivity analysis showed the model becomes untrustworthy above a 0.9 threshold, falling below chance." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Splitting Data: Once the images are preprocessed and converted into numerical arrays, we divide the dataset into three sets... Data Augmentation: To increase the diversity and robustness of the training dataset, data augmentation techniques, using the Image Data Generator module, was applied." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:bb59da535587> ;
            slr:claim_label "Augmentation correctly follows the split and is confined to training - better ordering than several neighbours - though rotation and flipping of scanpath traces produce examples that correspond to no possible viewing behaviour." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.86"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "A scanpath is a time and space based representation of a series of consecutive fixations and saccades that may overlap one another. [21] provides these visualised scanpath images which is used in the work as a biomarker to perform the classification task." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:ff89c89464cc> ;
            slr:claim_label "The input is a rendered picture of a gaze trajectory rather than the trajectory itself, so temporal information survives only as visual geometry and incidental graphical properties are available to the model alongside behavioural ones." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.92"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The ASD children were diagnosed by a team of clinicians consisted of a developmental-behavioral pediatrician and a child psychologist. Furthermore, they were evaluated by a child psychiatrist to validate the initial evaluation by the psychologist." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:628a8bb5f003> ;
            slr:claim_label "Diagnosis involved a three-clinician process but no standardised instrument." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The data used in this research is from a publicly available database. The information was gathered with informed consent. This research will not involve any personal information." ] ;
