        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "During model training, additional subject-level samples were generated by resampling scanpaths within each subject and recomputing the aggregated feature representation. This approach increases sample diversity while preserving subject-specific behavioral patterns." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.2> ;
            slr:claim_label "A within-subject resampling step is introduced whose placement relative to the fold split is not stated unambiguously, and which if applied before splitting would undermine the subject-wise protocol." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.93"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Note that the present study focusses on the recognition of diagnosis condition – as provided by clinicians – from speech recordings of AD, PDD-NOS, SLI, and TD children, which leads to a 4-way imbalanced classifcation task. Hence, performance is evaluated by unweighted average recall (UAR), which is suitable for imbalanced classes." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1145/3079452.3079492> ;
            slr:claim_label "The task is a four-way imbalanced classification evaluated by unweighted average recall against a 25% chance level." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "When no data augmentation was applied, the accuracy was approximately 60%. By employing seven data augmentation techniques, including noise addition, scaling, and flipping, the dataset was expanded, achieving an accuracy of 92%" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:3316ae46ffa0> ;
            slr:claim_label "The clearest single statement of augmentation-driven inflation in this review: a 32-point gain on a 100-sample corpus produced by augmentation alone, quoted here as motivating background rather than treated as a warning." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.98"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The movement of the child was not restricted and no obtrusive sensors were used. This means that this method can easily be generalized to other interactions from, for example, play time at home, where much larger datasets can be obtained." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1145/3371382.3378382> ;
            slr:claim_label "The design deliberately avoided movement restriction and wearable sensors to support generalisation to naturalistic settings." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In order to ensure accuracy, a top-down approach is adopted in this paper ... for the video captured by camera C1, YOLOv3 is used to achieve object detection. To improve detection accuracy, we do not use the weight pretrained on the COCO dataset, but train on our own dataset. More than 1700 images taken by 30 subjects are used to build our own object detection dataset." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:3dafd8b400d2> ;
            slr:claim_label "The one trained component of the pipeline was fitted on images of the same 30 children it is subsequently evaluated on, so the system has seen every participant in its own test set." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "For linear and quadratic classifiers, the AUCs were 0.67 and 0.71, respectively (Fig. 2C). ... SVM with radial basis function as kernels, which is a more complex classifier with nonlinearities, improved the overall classification performance (AUC 5 0.82) but also increased the variance (0.12), reflecting a degree of over-fitting to a specific training dataset." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:fcc0cc14d937> ;
            slr:claim_label "Cross-validated AUCs were 0.67, 0.71 and 0.82, with the SVM's gain explicitly attributed in part to overfitting." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Augmented data (7 geometric transformations: rotation, mirroring, scaling) were available for the Typical and Moderate ASD groups; only original recordings were used." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2026.1751654> ;
            slr:claim_label "Available augmentation was deliberately declined, a restraint several studies in this corpus do not exercise." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The predictions were obtained for individual 5s video segments and aggregated over the entire ADOS video for each subject from the two testing sets" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-021-94378-z> ;
            slr:claim_label "Segment-level predictions were aggregated to one prediction per child before performance was computed, avoiding the segment-level inflation seen elsewhere in this literature." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.98"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Note that performance in the unmatched sample is inflated by the inclusion of age/gender as features, given the disparity between groups in these factors. As such, the matched sample provides a better estimate of performance, despite its smaller size." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41398-026-03823-y> ;
            slr:claim_label "Matching on age and gender reduces accuracy from 81.8% to 74.0%, quantifying demographic confounding at roughly eight accuracy points - the only such measurement in the charted corpus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.99"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "when comparing ROC AUC of the optimal set of features using 10-fold (0.9344...) and the original 10-fold combined model (0.9235...), they were not significantly different according to DeLong's test (p = 0.1592)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1002/aur.2733> ;
            slr:claim_label "Recursive feature elimination produced no significant gain, and the higher selected-subset figure is reported as such rather than promoted." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the dataset includes thirteen boys, aged 10 to 16 years, diagnosed with ASD in the first group. The second group consists of four TD boys, aged 9 to 16 years." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.46604/aiti.2024.13951> ;
            slr:claim_label "Thirteen autistic and four typically developing children - the smallest comparison group in the review, setting a participant-level majority-class baseline of 76.5% against which the reported 89-94% is never compared." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.96"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The expression basis W used by 3DI method is constructed via PCA, which limits the interpretability as PCA components are not localized - we cannot associate any PCA component with a specific facial region. To make the results of our study more interpretable, we modified the expression model in a way that the resultant expression model, W', contains 60 localized basis components." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:7adb257effec> ;
            slr:claim_label "Interpretability treated as a design constraint: the representation was rebuilt before modelling so that features map to nameable facial regions, at a stated modelling cost." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.93"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The MobileNet model demonstrated outstanding performance in all parameters, attaining perfect precision, recall, and F1-score for both ASD and non-ASD classes... resulting in a remarkable overall accuracy of 100%." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:bb59da535587> ;
            slr:claim_label "The headline 100% is 55 of 55 test images correct, on an image-level split of a collection with repeated images per child." ;
