                    rdf:value "A controlled environment is a situation where researchers have a lot of control over factors that can affect the data being collected. To reduce potential sources of error or bias in the data, researchers adjust and control these variables. On the other hand, an uncontrolled environment is a situation where researchers have little to no control over a variety of factors." ] ;
