        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In the kinematic feature set, selected using a wrapped t-test, seven out of ten features were from the trials where movements were performed in elevated amplitude ... autistic individuals performed movements using a lower vertical amplitude than non-autistic individuals. As a consequence, autistic individuals also reached peak acceleration earlier in the" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-65384-4> ;
            slr:claim_label "Seven of ten selected features came from the elevated-amplitude condition, where autistic adults imitated with lower vertical amplitude and earlier peak acceleration." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "For the TD group, the feature related to biological movement was not selected. This fact can be explained by the generic construction of the feature... Considering that the attention of the TD group is specifically more focused on the regions with people and faces (already covered by the other features), the biological movement does not reveal itself as a discriminant feature" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-021-89023-8> ;
            slr:claim_label "Absence of the biological-movement feature from the typically developing model is explained as redundancy with face and person features rather than as absence of effect." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "While these ﬁndings are encouraging, LENA is not an open-source software and it is, therefore, not possible to further develop the LENA algorithms nor assess their utility in estimating ASD severity." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:f0fbf02fd04e> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors motivate building an open pipeline by the inability to inspect or extend the field's dominant commercial speech-analysis system." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In order to develop a model that minimizes data leakage from diagnosis to predictors, we included: (1) as predictors in the model measurements up to two years of age and (2) as the outcome metric of ASD, only children with an ASD diagnosis reported after two years of age." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:71fd566a4ffb> ;
            slr:claim_label "Temporal leakage from outcome to predictor is prevented by design rather than by assumption - the only study in the review that faces this problem and the only one that states an explicit control for it." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.96"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Behavior (1) was included to act as both a control (to ensure participants were not looking at the actor making the bid solely because he/she was looking at the participant) as well as a distractor ... Behavior (2) was included to act as a foil (a face that is not oriented toward the participant ... and the subtle hand movements served as a control for the speaking actor's mouth movements)" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1145/3539226> ;
            slr:claim_label "Explicit controls and foils built into the stimulus design to distinguish genuine social responsiveness from gaze-following and from mouth-movement salience - the most carefully reasoned stimulus construction in this corpus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.92"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the 10-fold cross-validation splits the data into 90 samples for training and 10 samples for testing in each learning. The averaged results were calculated from a total of 50 training runs (10 folds × 5 run)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:3316ae46ffa0> ;
