            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:e03dbcffcbc9> ;
            slr:claim_label "The only quantified leakage measurement in the facial-image branch, and it indicts the branch's standard practice: conventional frame-level splitting of this video-derived corpus leaves near-duplicate images across the train-test boundary." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.97"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The condition appears before the age of three and can last a lifetime, so people who are not diagnosed in childhood have a poorer quality of life." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:7d280d7f3a95> ;
            slr:claim_label "The paper is motivated throughout by detecting autism in young children, while its data are adult and adolescent social-media users on a platform with a minimum age of 13 - a mismatch never acknowledged." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.89"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "For the experiment was considered 252 users in which 221 are ASD users and 31 are not suffering from ASD. Before the pre-processing procedure, the dataset was conformed by 1,014,723 tweets that were already classified. After passing through the four mentioned steps, the dataset was reduced and cleaned up to 404,627 tweets. From the whole data, it is considered a sub-dataset in which there are 45,000 tweets from both ASD users and non-ASD users." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:7d280d7f3a95> ;
            slr:claim_label "The entire 45,000-tweet negative class comes from just 31 users, roughly 1,450 tweets each, against about 200 per autistic user - the imbalance that makes author recognition the model's most efficient route to high accuracy." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.99"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "for each participant four datasets were obtained: \"full variables\" (158), \"basic variables\" (24), \"prior variables\" (60), and \"secondary variables\" (72)... a partitioning of the data was performed, using a stratified five-folds methodology." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2025.1558621> ;
            slr:claim_label "Participant-level stratified cross-validation over feature sets containing up to 158 variables for 93 children, with the headline taken as the best across four sets and several algorithms." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "True positives/true negatives 28/16 False positives/false negatives 13/1 Accuracy [%] 75.9 Sensitivity [%] 96.6 Speciﬁcity [%] 55.2 Area under the curve 0.71" ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3389/frobt.2019.00132> ;
            slr:claim_label "Specificity was only 55.2%, with 13 of 29 controls misclassified as autistic." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Thus, the screening paradigm applied should not only be informative, but also short." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10803-018-3690-y> ;
            slr:claim_label "Paradigm brevity is framed as a design requirement for young children, motivating the 10-second stimulus." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "the model including all joints and virtual stimuli conditions showed the lowest accuracy (70.21%) and the lower true positives (45.45%)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/jcm9051260> ;
            slr:claim_label "Pooling all joints across all stimulus conditions produced the worst performance of any configuration, with sensitivity below 50%." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Although using the responsive social smile score alone cannot give a very comprehensive ASD classiﬁcation, we believe that fusing scores and features from multiple automatic assessment tasks can further enhance the overall ASD screening performance." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.1109/ICPR48806.2021.9412766> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors state that a single protocol cannot support comprehensive autism classification and propose fusion across multiple automated protocols." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "The 'playing only with the wheels' state is when the sensorized toy car is almost motionless while its wheels are rotating. In this case, the shaft encoders show changes while there is no significant change in the acceleration values. This state exactly represents the interest in rotating objects and objects' rotation." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/su15107790> ;
            slr:claim_label "The core sensing insight: two cheap sensors that are individually ambiguous become jointly interpretable, defining a four-state behavioural budget from an unstructured play session." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.91"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "Participants were 457 toddlers, 17–36 months of age, who were recruited from four pediatric primary care clinics during a well-child checkup. Forty-one toddlers were subsequently diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder (ASD) based on DSM-5 criteria." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:dbb27be8e821> ;
            slr:claim_label "Recruitment was consecutive from routine primary care with diagnosis ascertained afterwards, giving a prevalence-realistic 41:416 class ratio." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.95"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "no differences in EEG were found in some previous studies, especially for high functioning autism. We think the reason is that ASD is a complex disease with large individual differences... Therefore, using only EEG evaluation may be insufficient to identify children with this complex disease." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <urn:slr:article:3ba88bcdc38e> ;
            slr:claim_label "The authors motivate fusion by arguing that EEG abnormalities are inconsistent across the autism spectrum, particularly in high-functioning presentations." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.9"^^xsd:float ],
        [ a oa:Annotation ;
            oa:hasBody [ a dcterms:Text ;
                    rdf:value "In contrast to the previously reported studies, we evaluate the model performance using the area under the ROC curve (AUC), specificity, sensitivity, positive predictive value (PPV), and negative prediction value (NPV)." ] ;
            oa:hasTarget <https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics12020518> ;
            slr:claim_label "The metric panel is an explicit departure from the field's convention of reporting accuracy alone." ;
            slr:relevance_score "0.85"^^xsd:float ] ;
