            slr:decision "include" ;
            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a primary computational study reported to STARD standards: a prospective diagnostic study of 110 children aged 24-72 months across multiple South Korean sites, of whom 95 were analysed (45 autistic, 50 typically developing); K-CARS-2 screening for all, K-ADOS-2 and child psychiatrist diagnosis for the autism group, and cognitive assessment with Korean Bayley-II or K-WPPSI-IV; a purpose-built three-task joint attention protocol derived from the Early Social Communication Scales, video-recorded in a single 10-minute session; a CNN-LSTM-attention architecture evaluated by 10-fold group-wise (by individual) cross-validation with AUROC, accuracy, precision and recall reported with confidence intervals; and Grad-CAM, attention plots and hierarchical clustering for interpretation. Eligible on all criteria." ;
