            slr:assessed_on "full_text" ;
            slr:decision "include" ;
            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a primary study collecting original data: 1,500 thermal images from 30 male autistic children aged 5 to 15 at Don Guanella Special School in Chennai, captured with a FLIR USB thermal camera at emissivity 0.98 across four settings - outdoor play, classroom, dining area and veranda - plus 20 videos for real-time testing. Facial expression and skin-temperature dynamics are behavioural and physiological correlates of observable state, within the review's modality scope. Included, with the qualification that the classification target is a three-level severity grade rather than diagnosis, that no non-autistic comparison group exists, and that the source of the severity labels is nowhere stated." ;
