            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a secondary analysis of the Khozaei et al. cry corpus collected in Iran: 62 children aged 18 to 54 months, 31 autistic and 31 typically developing, 24 boys and 7 girls in each group, with roughly six cry instances per child. Praat-derived perturbation measures were compared statistically between groups and a recurrent convolutional network was trained on cry spectrograms. Crying is vocal behaviour the child produces and is within the review's modality scope; the study also occupies a distinct position in the corpus as the only one analysing pre-linguistic vocalisation as such." ;
