            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms 20 children with high-functioning autism and 23 age-matched typically developing children, LeapMotion capture of an oscillatory hand-movement task, entropy and 95%-range kinematic complexity features, five classifiers under leave-one-out cross-validation, and reported accuracy, sensitivity, specificity and AUC." ;
            slr:full_text_source "user_supplied_pdf" ;
            slr:screening_stage "full_text" ],
        [ a prov:Activity,
                slr:ScreeningDecisionRecord ;
            dcterms:title "Hybrid weight optimized deep learning for autism and visual sensory processing disorder detection: A heuristic strategy on medical domain" ;
            bibo:pmid "local_5a7ab52d" ;
            slr:assessed_on "full_text" ;
            slr:decision "include" ;
            slr:decision_rationale "Included on a narrow reading and charted with the record that the study is largely uninterpretable. A behavioural modality is present - seven facial emotion probabilities (angry, disgust, fear, happy, neutral, sad, surprise) plus derived positive and negative emotion scores - alongside two physiological variables, heart rate and body temperature, and the prediction target is a binary 'autism and visual SPD detection' label. That meets the letter of the eligibility criteria. However, the full text contains no participant count, no demographics, no recruitment description, no diagnostic procedure, no ethics statement and no consent statement; the data are described only as 'collected manually' from 'various subjects'; and the target conflates autism with visual sensory processing disorder into a single undifferentiated label. It is retained because the review should record the existence and characteristics of this segment of the literature, and because the one worked data table the paper provides is itself informative about what the reported 96.4% accuracy is likely to reflect." ;
            slr:full_text_source "user_supplied_pdf" ;
            slr:screening_stage "full_text" ],
        [ a prov:Activity,
                slr:ScreeningDecisionRecord ;
            dcterms:title "Eye gaze as a biomarker in the recognition of autism spectrum disorder using virtual reality and machine learning: A proof of concept for diagnosis" ;
            bibo:pmid "local_36617ec5" ;
            slr:assessed_on "title_abstract" ;
            slr:decision "include" ;
            slr:decision_rationale "Multivariate supervised machine learning applied to eye gaze features recorded in an immersive virtual environment to recognise autism - a computational model on behavioral data with an autism recognition target." ;
            slr:screening_stage "title_abstract" ],
        [ a prov:Activity,
                slr:ScreeningDecisionRecord ;
            dcterms:title "Large-scale Investigations of AAC Usage Patterns: Trends, Autism, and Stacked Autoencoders" ;
            bibo:pmid "local_7c6a5aa4" ;
            slr:assessed_on "full_text" ;
            slr:decision "include" ;
            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a primary computational study: usage logs from 6,033 users of the FreeSpeech iPad AAC application collected between January 2012 and May 2014, comprising over 2.5 million button presses, of which 5,372 users had valid usage patterns and 180 disclosed a diagnosis through a voluntary online survey (81 autistic, 99 non-autistic); key presses and app events encoded as pseudo-semantic numeric identifiers and modelled sequentially, temporally and spectrally over fixed windows; classification with SVMs, probabilistic neural networks, logistic regression, stacked autoencoders and deep belief networks; and k-means pseudo-labelling used to extend the labelled set. Eligible on all criteria, with substantial caveats about the self-reported reference standard and the pseudo-labelling step recorded in the charting." ;
            slr:full_text_source "user_supplied_pdf" ;
            slr:screening_stage "full_text" ],
        [ a prov:Activity,
