            slr:assessed_on "full_text" ;
            slr:decision "include" ;
            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a primary computational study: 20 autistic and 21 typically developing children aged 6-13 filmed from a fixed side-view camera during a structured conversation with an interviewer at 80 cm; motion energy analysis extracting whole-body movement time series for both parties from manually drawn regions of interest; cross wavelet analysis producing coherence at 23 time scales; a pseudo-pair surrogate control constructed by pairing each child with an adult from a different video; four classifiers with forward feature selection evaluated by participant-level leave-one-out cross-validation; and reporting of accuracy, sensitivity, specificity and ROC curves. Eligible on all criteria. Charted with the note that this is a further analysis of the same participant cohort and recordings already charted in this review under a different modality (Zhao et al., oculomotor behaviour), which makes the two records directly comparable." ;
