            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a primary computational study on ABIDE-I: 1,112 subjects (539 autistic, 573 control) from 17 international sites, combining T1-weighted structural MRI processed by a CNN-GNN over the Harvard-Oxford atlas with approximately 65-70 tabular phenotype fields processed by GAMI-Net, fused through an autoencoder into a 32-dimensional latent space and classified by a hypernetwork-generated multilayer perceptron. Included as part of the verified corpus. The record notes that neither modality is behavioural data in the instrumental sense that most of this review covers - the imaging is neuroanatomical and the tabular fields are diagnostic-instrument scores rather than observations of what a person does - so the study is charted as the corpus's principal representative of the neuroimaging-plus-phenotype branch, and its findings are interpreted accordingly." ;
