            slr:decision_rationale "Title and abstract describe a computer-vision method combining human pose tracking, head pose estimation and automatic speech-based name detection to judge the response-to-name behaviour of autistic children, reporting 93.3% consistency with clinical diagnosis across 30 subjects and framing the work as an aid to early autism screening. A behavioural modality and a computational model are clearly present, but the sample is 29 autistic children and 1 typically developing child, and the target appears to be a behavioural response judgement rather than a diagnosis, so full-text assessment was needed to determine whether an autism prediction, screening, classification or severity-estimation target exists." ;
