            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a primary computational study on a purpose-built corpus: 3,137,952 tweets from 17,323 users who used #ActuallyAutistic and carried autism-related keywords in their profile descriptions, against 3,377,518 tweets from 171,273 control users, collected across 2014-2022 and analysed with TF-IDF and word2vec representations, classical classifiers and an attention-based bidirectional LSTM, with user-level splitting. Naturally produced written language is behaviour the person generated, which places the study within the review's modality scope alongside the speech and conversation studies. The label is self-identification through hashtag use rather than clinical diagnosis, which is a reference-standard limitation charted below rather than an eligibility failure - and one the authors state themselves, describing their target as 'use of the #ActuallyAutistic hashtag, an imperfect proxy for self-reported autism'." ;
