            slr:decision_rationale "Included at the boundary of the review's modality scope and charted, like the companion study on the same dataset, as a negative exemplar. The input is 2,936 static facial photographs from the same publicly scraped Kaggle collection already charted in this review, in which autistic images are drawn from autism-focused online sources and non-autistic images gathered separately - so the modality is facial appearance rather than behaviour, despite the title's framing as 'emotion-based'. No emotion or expression analysis of any kind is performed anywhere in the paper. It is retained because the review must characterise the size and reporting conventions of this branch of the literature, and because this study adds a specific and instructive feature to the picture: an exhaustive comparison of feature families and classifiers reported without any statement of how training and test data were separated." ;
            slr:full_text_source "user_supplied_pdf" ;
            slr:screening_stage "full_text" ],
        [ a prov:Activity,
                slr:ScreeningDecisionRecord ;
            dcterms:title "The Impact of Speaker Diarization on DNN-based Autism Severity Estimation" ;
            bibo:pmid "local_988c462e" ;
            slr:assessed_on "title_abstract" ;
            slr:decision "include" ;
            slr:decision_rationale "A speech-based system combining automatic speaker diarization with a convolutional network to estimate autism severity scores from ADOS recordings, with correlation against clinician-assigned scores reported." ;
            slr:screening_stage "title_abstract" ],
        [ a prov:Activity,
                slr:ScreeningDecisionRecord ;
            dcterms:title "Social robot in diagnosis of autism among preschool children" ;
            bibo:pmid "local_c6f1209b" ;
            slr:assessed_on "full_text" ;
            slr:decision "include" ;
            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a primary pilot study: preschool children with autism playing two purpose-designed games ('Touch me' and 'Dance with me') with a NAO humanoid robot, video-recorded and scored by competent raters against a questionnaire, with a within-group comparison of instructed against spontaneous behaviour by Wilcoxon signed-rank test. Included as part of the verified corpus, and charted with the record made explicit that no computational model is fitted, no comparison group is present, and no individual is classified - the study is a pilot establishing the paradigm and the engineering requirements, and its substantive contribution is the within-group dissociation between instructed and spontaneous turn-taking." ;
            slr:full_text_source "user_supplied_pdf" ;
            slr:screening_stage "full_text" ],
        [ a prov:Activity,
                slr:ScreeningDecisionRecord ;
