            bibo:pmid "local_f1b626c8" ;
            slr:assessed_on "full_text" ;
            slr:decision "include" ;
            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a primary computational study: 20 autistic boys recruited from a rehabilitation clinic in Tehran and 20 boys from a public elementary school, a two-stage computer game built on the JAFFE facial-expression database, stationary eye tracking, an 18-feature matrix of fixation counts and fixation durations over defined screen regions, and a MATLAB multilayer perceptron with scaled conjugate gradient training evaluated by confusion matrix with precision, accuracy, sensitivity, specificity and ROC curves across four feature subsets. Eligible on all criteria. Charted with the caveat, established by arithmetic on the reported percentages, that the modelled units are 240 game observations rather than 40 children and that the headline figures are totals across training, validation and test rather than held-out performance (see rubric and appraisal)." ;
