            slr:assessed_on "full_text" ;
            slr:decision "include" ;
            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a primary computational study on two image corpora: the Piosenka Kaggle facial-photograph dataset (2,866 images, 1,433 per class, ages 1-11) and the YTUIA dataset of face crops extracted with MTCNN from the Self-Stimulatory Behaviours Dataset YouTube videos (1,163 images after preprocessing). Models are SE-CNN and SE-MSF-CNN with white shark optimisation, evaluated within each dataset and, unusually for this branch, across datasets in both directions. Included, with the qualification recorded throughout this review for the Piosenka corpus: the paper states directly that the autism images were 'taken from websites and Facebook pages that included autism-related content', so class membership is confounded with image provenance. The study is nonetheless charted rather than excluded, because it is the only paper in the facial-photograph branch to conduct an explicit leakage investigation and to report cross-dataset transfer - both of which bear on the review's methodological synthesis." ;
