            slr:decision_rationale "Full text confirms a secondary-analysis computational study on the Kaggle autistic-children facial image corpus - 2,940 RGB images of children aged 2 to 14, 1,327 labelled autistic and 1,613 non-autistic - with three ImageNet-pretrained architectures compared under an 80/10/10 image-level split. This is the sixth study in the review built on this corpus family. Included, with the qualification recorded throughout: the paper states directly that the non-autistic images were 'randomly retrieved from web searches', so class membership is confounded with image provenance." ;
