                    slr:outcome "Accuracy, sensitivity, specificity and F1, each plotted against training percentage and iteration count. The definitions given are partly incorrect: accuracy is defined as dividing the total number of instances by the number of correctly classified instances - the reciprocal of accuracy - and specif" ] ;
            slr:section_g_synthesis [ a slr:SynthesisFields ;
                    slr:summary_of_findings "Accuracy 95.3%, sensitivity 96.5%, specificity 94.8%. Intermediate values on the curves include accuracy 0.927 at 70% training data and iteration 20." ] ] ;
