<https://doi.org/10.1145/3806026> a fabio:Expression,
        slr:IncludedSource ;
    dcterms:abstract "Explainable Children Autism Detection using Gaze Features in Audio-Visual Speech Comprehension MIGUEL ZARAGOZÁ-PORTOLÉS, Universitat Politècnica de València, Spain DAVID GIMENO-GOMEZ, Universitat Politècnica de València, Spain VICENTA ÁVILA, University of Valencia, Spain DR. INMACULADA FAJARDO, University of Valencia, Spain DR. ANTONIO FERRER, University of Valencia, Spain NADINA GOMEZ-MERINO, University of Valencia, Spain NOEMI SKROBISZEWSKA, University of Valencia, Spain CARLOS-D. MARTÍNEZ-HINAREJOS, Universitat Politècnica de València, Spain Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD) is a neurodevelopmental condition marked by impairments in social interac- tion and delayed language acquisition. Early and accurate identification is crucial for timely interventions that support cognitive and social development. Motivated by the subjectivity of traditional behavior-based assessments, computational methodologies offer more objective and cost-effective alternatives. Among these, eye-tracking stands out for capturing subtle attentional and perceptual patterns. This paper investigates the use of eye-tracking data for automatic ASD detection in children during audio-visual storytelling interactions, emphasizing traditional yet explainable machine learning methods. Although performance remains modest, our analyses reveal that fixation duration and revisit patterns to facial regions may serve as potential biomark- ers. Further analyses highlight the impact of stimulus modality, suggesting that the inclusion of visual speech cues provides valuable discriminative information. These findings have the potential to support and guide the work of psychologists in the assessment of ASD within speech comprehension contexts. CCS Concepts: • Computing methodologies →Supervised learning by classification; • Human- centered computing →Empirical studies in HCI; • Applied computing →Health informatics. Additional Key Words and Phrases: Austism spectrum disorder, Early identification in children, Eye-tracking, Audio-visual speech comprehension, Explainable Artificial Intelligence ACM Reference Format: Miguel Zaragozá-Portolés, David Gimeno-Gomez, Vicenta Ávila, Dr. Inmaculada Fajardo, Dr. Antonio Ferrer, Nadina Gomez-Merino, Noemi Skrobiszewska, and Carlos-D. Martínez-Hinarejos. 2026. Explainable Children Autism Detection using Gaze Features in Audio-Visual Speech Comprehension. Proc. ACM Hum.-Comput. Interact. 10, 3, Article ETRA012 (May 2026), 18 pages. https://doi.org/10.1145/3806026 Authors’ Contact Information: Miguel Zaragozá-Portolés, Pattern Recognition and Human Language Technology Research Center (PRHLT), Universitat Politècnica de València, Valencia, Spain, mizapor@inf.upv.es; David Gimeno-Gomez, Pattern Recognition and Human Language Technology research center (PRHLT), Universitat Politècnica de València, Valencia, Spain, dagigo1@dsic.upv.es; Vicenta Ávila, Reading Research Unit (ERI LECTURA), University of Valencia, Valencia, Spain, vicenta.avila@uv.es; Dr. Inmaculada Fajardo, Reading Research Unit/ Dept. Developmental and Educational Psychology, University of Valencia, Valencia, Spain, inmaculada.fajardo@uv.es; Dr. Antonio Ferrer, Reading Research Unit/ Dept. Developmental and Educational Psychology, University of Valencia, Valencia, Spain, antonio.ferrer@uv.es; Nadina Gomez- Merino, Reading Research Unit, University of Valencia, Valencia, Spain, nadina.gomez@uv.es; Noemi Skrobiszewska, Reading Research Unit (ERI LECTURA), University of Valencia, Valencia, Spain, noemi.skrobiszewska@uv.es; Carlos-D. Martínez-Hinarejos, Pattern Recognition and Human Language Technologies Research Center, Universitat Politècnica de València, València, Spain, cmartine@dsic.upv.es. This work is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s). ACM 2573-0142/2026/5-ARTETRA012 https://doi.org/10.1145/3806026 Proc. ACM Hum.-Comput. Interact., Vol. 10, No. 3, Article ETRA012. Publication date: May 2026." ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Zaragozá-Portolés M; Gimeno-Gomez D; Ávila V; Fajardo DI; Ferrer DA; Gomez-Merino N; Skrobiszewska N; Martínez-Hinarejos CD (2026). Explainable Children Autism Detection using Gaze Features in Audio-Visual Speech Comprehension. **. https://doi.org/10.1145/3806026" ;
