    dcterms:abstract "TYPE Original Research PUBLISHED 24 June 2025 DOI 10.3389/fnins.2025.1558621 OPEN ACCESS EDITED BY Dongchuan Yu, Southeast University, Nanjing, China REVIEWED BY Brahim Benabderrahmane, University of Constantine 2, Algeria Judy Simon, SRM Arts and Science College, India *CORRESPONDENCE Adoración Antolí aantoli@uco.es RECEIVED 13 January 2025 ACCEPTED 20 May 2025 PUBLISHED 24 June 2025 CITATION Antolí A, Rodriguez-Lozano FJ, Cañas JJ, Vacas J, Cuadrado F, Sánchez-Raya A, Pérez-Dueñas C and Gámez-Granados JC (2025) Using explainable machine learning and eye-tracking for diagnosing autism spectrum and developmental language disorders in social attention tasks. Front. Neurosci. 19:1558621. doi: 10.3389/fnins.2025.1558621 COPYRIGHT © 2025 Antolí, Rodriguez-Lozano, Cañas, Vacas, Cuadrado, Sánchez-Raya, Pérez-Dueñas and Gámez-Granados. This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License (CC BY). The use, distribution or reproduction in other forums is permitted, provided the original author(s) and the copyright owner(s) are credited and that the original publication in this journal is cited, in accordance with accepted academic practice. No use, distribution or reproduction is permitted which does not comply with these terms. Using explainable machine learning and eye-tracking for diagnosing autism spectrum and developmental language disorders in social attention tasks Adoración Antolí1,2*, Francisco Javier Rodriguez-Lozano3, José Juan Cañas4, Julia Vacas1,2, Fátima Cuadrado1,2, Araceli Sánchez-Raya1,2, Carolina Pérez-Dueñas1,2 and Juan Carlos Gámez-Granados3 1Department of Psychology, University of Córdoba, Córdoba, Spain, 2Maimónides Biomedical Research Institute of Córdoba, Córdoba, Spain, 3Department of Electronic and Computer Engineering, Higher Polytechnic School, University of Córdoba., Córdoba, Spain, 4Mind, Brain and Behavioral Research Center, University of Granada, Granada, Spain" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Antolí A; Rodriguez-Lozano FJ; Juan Cañas J; Vacas J; Cuadrado F; Sánchez-Raya A; Pérez-Dueñas C; Gámez-Granados JC (2025). Using explainable machine learning and eye-tracking for diagnosing autism spectrum and developmental language disorders in social attention tasks. **. https://doi.org/10.3389/fnins.2025.1558621" ;
    dcterms:creator "Antolí A",
        "Cuadrado F",
